    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "MYROBALANS: The dried fruits of different varieties of terminalia. The fruit, varying from the size of an olive to that of a gall-nut, consists of a white pentangular nut, covered by a substance about 2 lines in thickness. The latter, which is the only valuable part, is mucilaginous and highly astringent; and being separated from the nut is employed, with th..."@en ;
